# --- build artifacts ---
# build*/ (not build/): every variant gets its OWN object directory -- build-artless,
# build-delta, build-sd, build-artless-noperf ... Those used to stay invisible only because
# every file inside them happened to match *.o/*.d below; the Makefile now also generates
# build*/pdna_git.h (the build stamp), which does not. The trailing slash keeps build.sh out.
build*/
*.elf
*.elf.stackcache.json
*.gba
*.map
*.o
*.d
*.i
*.s
*.log

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store

# --- local-only assets (NOT redistributed; see README + tools/gen_icons.py) ---
# Ripped Gen-3 sprite pack (© Game Freak / The Pokémon Company)
/assets/sprites/
# Ripped Gen-3 PC-storage hand cursor (regenerate with: python3 tools/gen_hand.py)
/assets/storage/
/source/hand_cursor.c
/source/hand_cursor.h
# Ripped Gen-3 type-label badges (regenerate with: python3 tools/gen_types.py)
/assets/types/
/source/type_icons.c
# Ripped Gen-3 item icons (regenerate with: python3 tools/gen_items.py)
/assets/items/
/source/item_icons.c
/source/item_icons_data.s
# Sparse clones of pret/pokeruby + pret/pokefirered (reference/art staging only)
/assets/upstream
# Ripped Emerald bag-screen art (regenerate with: python3 tools/gen_bag_bg.py)
/assets/bag/
/source/bag_bg.c
/source/bag_bg_data.s
# Ripped Emerald trainer-card art (regenerate with: python3 tools/gen_card_bg.py)
/assets/card/
/source/card_bg.c
/source/card_bg_data.s
# Ripped RS/Emerald Pokeblock-case art (regenerate: python3 tools/gen_pokeblock_bg.py)
/assets/pokeblock/
/source/pokeblock_bg.c
/source/pokeblock_bg_data.s
# Generated icon art blobs (regenerate with: python3 tools/gen_icons.py)
/source/mon_icons.c
/data/icons.*
/data/*.bin
# Generated hardware-OAM box-icon art (regenerate: python3 tools/gen_icons_oam.py)
/source/mon_icons_oam.c
/source/mon_icons_oam_data.s
# Generated hardware-OAM hand cursor (regenerate: python3 tools/gen_hand_oam.py)
# NOTE: the art *.h headers are COMMITTED now (canonical API; the artless build
# relies on them + source/art_fallbacks.c). Only the generated DATA (.c/.s) stays ignored.
/source/hand_oam.c

# --- real save files (personal / copyrighted game data) ---
*.sav
*.sav.bak*

# --- pret decompilation excerpts (unlicensed; reference only, not shipped) ---
/reference/
# generated front/back sprites (ripped art) + data tables — regenerate locally
/source/mon_front.c
/source/mon_front_data.s
/source/mon_back.c
/source/mon_back_data.s
/source/mon_icons_data.s
/source/data_tables.c
# the 741 verbatim Game Freak description strings, split out of data_tables.c
# (BACKLOG #19 / docs/AUDIT-2026-09-05-backlog-3-19.md section B) — see desc_gate.h
/source/data_desc.c
/source/learnsets.c
# wild-encounter tables read out of the user's own cart dumps (tools/gen_encounters.py)
/source/encounters.c
# script-placed Pokemon (setwildbattle/givemon), likewise from the cart dumps
# (tools/gen_statics.py) — the other half of "how is this Pokemon obtained"
/source/statics.c
# forward evolution index + per-species minimum level, likewise from the cart dumps
# (tools/gen_evolutions.py)
/source/evolutions.c
# per-game move-source tables extracted from the pret decomps (tools/gen_learnsets2.py)
/source/learnsets2.c
# per-game Gen-1/2 field-offset + named-event-flag tables (BACKLOG #49 P0,
# tools/gen_gbfields.py) — source/gb_fields_fallback.c / gb_flags_fallback.c are the
# COMMITTED weak fallback so a clone that never ran the generator still links.
/source/gb1_base_gen.c
/source/gb_fields.c
/source/gb_flags.c
/source/wallpapers.c
/source/daycare_bg_data.h

# Local daycare-map working folder: pokeemerald decomp (reference-only/unlicensed),
# porymap, and a real ROM/save. Never commit any of it.
daycare map/

# on-hardware /PokeDNA/log.txt drops (local evidence, not shipped)
logs/

# tools/gb_roundtrip.py --selftest output: SCREENSHOTS OF RETAIL POKEMON GAMES, taken by
# booting a real ROM in mGBA to prove an edited save still loads. Local evidence only —
# every frame is Game Freak's copyrighted artwork and this repo is public GPLv3 with an
# IP-cleanliness gate. Ignored so `git add -A` can never stage them.
gb_roundtrip_out/

# internal session/analysis notes (local-only; never published)
docs/analysis-*/
docs/audit-*
docs/*CONTINUATION-PROMPT.md
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/SESSION_SUMMARY.md
/data/
tools/__pycache__/

# compiler stack-usage reports (-fstack-usage build output)
*.su

# Engineering / process notes — local only, not part of the shipped tool.
# (Guy 2026-08-03: "the engineering are also local only, they are not related
#  to the end product".) They stay on disk; git just stops carrying them.
docs/
.claude/
__pycache__/

# Game Boy cartridge dumps + their battery saves (Guy's own: Red/Yellow/Gold/Crystal).
# They live OUTSIDE this repo at gba-toolkit/roms/gb/ (itself gitignored) — these
# patterns are belt-and-braces so a stray copy inside the project can never be added.
*.gb
*.gbc
*.pk2
*.sav.dat
/roms/

# PDNA_EMIT_PLANT=1 test output (BACKLOG #150 S150-2 step 6): raw 2400-byte Bank box
# files emitted by tests/host_bankcell_test.c for a real-hardware SD-card copy, never
# by default and never committed.
/box14.box
/box15.box

# BACKLOG #179 Phase A: tools/vsd_img.c-built virtual-SD card images -- they embed
# whatever fixture .pds/.sav bytes a chain seeded into them (personal save data in
# real usage), and tools/vsd_img.c list/vsd_diff.py's own `path size crc32` output
# files. Both live under /tmp/pokedna-vsd/ (design S4.6) and are never committed.
*.img
*.list

# macOS sed -i -E backups
*-E

# emulator savestates / battery saves (never commit)
*.ss[0-9]
*.sgm
*.srm
*.sa[0-9]
*.sav.*
